body: "## Problem\n\npm-web#305 binds project **deletion** to the storage pin captured at admission: the physical parent, the leaf device and inode, and re-verification before eviction and removal. Two other project-storage paths still act through the logical project path:\n\n1. **Initialization follow-ups and failed-init cleanup** (review thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c628Rhm, Major). `initProject` runs `workspace init` on the pinned storage, but `configureLocalOllamaSearch(dir)` and `ensureGraphExtension(userId, slug)` then resolve the logical path again. If the alias is retargeted in between, one initialization writes to two storage targets. If initialization throws, `removeOwnedProject` re-pins the logical path and can remove whatever it resolves to at cleanup time, instead of the storage that initialization created.\n2. **Authorized reads** (PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c628Rhi, Minor). The post-queue read binding compares the grant, workspace path and tracker path, but not the captured entry stamps. A directory renamed and recreated at the same path while a read waits in the queue passes the recheck, and the read then uses the replacement.\n\nBoth behave like `main`, which pins nothing on these paths. #305 improves deletion, and this issue extends the same guarantee to every project-storage access.\n\n## Expected\n\n- `initProject` returns its pin. The settings write (Ollama search), the graph extension install and failed-init cleanup all receive that pin and act through its physical parent and leaf. A mismatch refuses and records the cleanup as pending, and never removes a different target.\n- The read binding includes the captured entry stamps, so the post-queue recheck refuses a replaced directory with a 409.\n- One helper validates a pin before any project-storage access, so read, write and remove cannot drift.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Retargeting the alias between `workspace init` and the follow-ups refuses, and the alias target's settings and tracker are unchanged, byte for byte.\n- An init failure after a retarget leaves the other project's storage untouched.\n- A read whose directory is renamed and recreated while queued answers 409.\n- Normal init, read and delete behave as today, on the disposable test database only."
